   "is_new": true,
   "source": {
    "label": "The:regSubG",
    "number": "Theorem 3",
    "quote": "Consider the Gaussian process bandit problem. Under Assumptions~\\ref{Ass1},~\\ref{ass4}, and~(\\ref{Ass2} or~\\ref{Ass3}), for $\\delta\\in(0,1)$, with probability at least $1-\\delta$, MVR satisfies r^{MVR}_N \\le \\sqrt{\\frac{2\\gamma_N}{\\log(1+\\frac{1}{\\lambda^2})N}}(2B+\\beta(\\frac{\\delta}{3}) + \\beta(...)) + \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{N}}, where under Assumption~\\ref{Ass2}, $\\beta(\\delta) = \\frac{R}{\\lambda} \\sqrt{2\\log(\\frac{1}{\\delta})}$"
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "N is T. beta substituted explicitly for sub-Gaussian case. Remark 2 simplifies to O(sqrt(gamma_N log(N^d/delta)/N)). MVR exploration does not depend on N, budget may be unknown, so anytime. delta enters analysis only (not algorithm)."
  },
